---
description: RLM onboarding questions during initial project setup
alwaysApply: true
---

When initializing this template, configuring a new project or moving it to another
developer workstation, follow `docs/rlm-setup.md` together with `TEMPLATE.md`.
Ask whether to enable personal RLM; offer project registration with a verified
dump path and separately offer index creation. Ask for the user's RLM project
password only when needed; never invent, log or commit it. Existing matching
registrations must be reused. Missing server or dump must be reported explicitly.
Graph/code-metadata availability does not suppress these onboarding questions.
This setup exception does not change the source-search fallback rules.

On dev-workplaces, RLM is preinstalled and the managed local service enables
passwordless operations. Do not ask for a password there unless the actual server
response requires one. Never retry mutations blindly after a password challenge.
For setup, inspect only the known export path from local config (otherwise src/cf),
MCP connection and registry. Do not recursively search the home directory for dumps,
install packages or research RLM architecture. If the dump is empty, report this
immediately and offer export as a separate action; indexing must wait for sources.

For index lifecycle decisions after onboarding, follow `docs/rlm-setup.md`:
check index info at setup and before RLM source search. Offer build for a missing
index only when sources exist. After a successful export or Git update that
changed the registered dump, offer incremental update for an existing index.
Do not update after unrelated changes, failed exports or while a job is running.
Explicit per-project consent may authorize future updates after successful exports;
record its scope in ignored local memory.md. It never authorizes build, drop,
rebuild or updates after Git operations. Report background job completion or error
using info; accepting a job is not proof that indexing has completed.
